---
import Footer from "../../components/shared/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../../components/shared/Header.astro";
import PageHeader from "../../components/shared/PageHeader.astro";
import ContactBanner from "../../components/shared/ContactBanner.astro";
import LeadBlock from "../../components/shared/LeadBlock.astro";
import FloorPlanDiagram from "../../components/case-studies/FloorPlanDiagram.astro";
import VideoCallDiagram from "../../components/case-studies/VideoCallDiagram.astro";
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Yembo Case Study: Engineering for an AI Platform | Novage"
  canonical="case-studies/yembo"
  description="Seven years as engineering partner to Yembo, an AI company for moving and insurance in 40+ countries: full-stack, mobile apps, 3D, video calls and AI."
>
  <Header />
  <div id="content">
    <article>
      <PageHeader
        eyebrow="Case study"
        title="Yembo"
        accent="Long-term engineering partner for an AI platform"
      >
        <p class="lead">
          <a href="https://www.yembo.ai/">Yembo</a> builds AI for the moving and
          insurance industries. We are its long-term engineering partner,
          working alongside Yembo's core team across web, backend, mobile and
          QA.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a
            class="button primary"
            href="#contact"
            data-umami-event="yembo-discuss"
          >
            Discuss your project
          </a>
        </div>
      </PageHeader>

      <div class="page container content">
        <ul class="key-facts">
          <li>
            <strong>40+</strong> countries using the platform
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Millions</strong> of videos processed
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>7 years</strong> of engineering partnership
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>10+</strong> people today, up from 1 engineer in 2019
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>About Yembo</h2>
        <p>
          Yembo is a venture-backed company building what it calls "spatial
          intelligence for every property." It started in the moving industry,
          where its AI understands images and videos of a home for virtual
          surveys, and has grown into insurance, with AI-powered 3D home
          inspections for claims and underwriting, and into property management.
          Yembo holds 10+ granted AI patents.
        </p>

        <h2>The engagement</h2>
        <p>
          The partnership started in 2019 with a single engineer and grew into a
          team across web, backend, mobile and QA. Today we build most of the
          user interface of Yembo's SaaS platforms for{" "}
          <a href="https://yembo.ai/moving">moving</a> and{" "}
          <a href="https://yembo.ai/insurance">insurance</a>, and a large part
          of the backend. Product direction comes from Yembo, and its CTO often
          designs the backend as well. Our team takes responsibility for the
          applications and modules it owns, and works with Yembo's core team
          from the first design discussions to production.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Technology stack:</strong> React, TypeScript and JavaScript,
          React Native, Swift, Kotlin, Node.js, PHP, AWS and Playwright.
        </p>

        <h2>Turning ideas into features with Yembo's core team</h2>
        <p>
          Most ideas start at Yembo: its CTO designs prototypes and sets the
          technical direction. We help turn them into production features that
          hold up under real use and scale.
        </p>

        <h3>AI in the product, including live video calls</h3>
        <p>
          We integrate AI solutions into Yembo's products — both models
          developed in-house by Yembo's core team and services from outside
          vendors — so that AI results reach users as working product features.
        </p>
        <p>
          A key example is{" "}
          <a href="https://yembo.ai/moving/surveys">Smart Consult</a>, Yembo's
          live video consultation: the homeowner joins from their phone in one
          click, the mover guides the walkthrough, and the AI builds the
          inventory while they talk. Together with Yembo's core team, we develop
          the video calls and integrate AI into them:{" "}
          <strong>live AI object detection</strong>, which recognizes items as
          the camera moves through the home, and <strong>Teleprompter</strong>,
          an AI mentor that prompts the mover with the right follow-up question
          during the call. Combined, they help movers on the platform increase
          their deal closure rates.
        </p>
        <figure class="diagram-figure">
          <VideoCallDiagram />
          <figcaption>
            An illustration of the idea: as the homeowner's camera moves through
            the room, AI object detection adds each item to the inventory, and
            Teleprompter suggests the mover's next question.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <h3>A 3D home editor for insurance claims</h3>
        <p>
          With Yembo's{" "}
          <a href="https://yembo.ai/insurance/claims">ScanMyHome®</a>,
          policyholders, inspectors and adjusters scan a home on their phone,
          and Yembo's AI 3D pipeline turns the scan into a 3D model of the
          house. Our part starts there: we built the in-browser 3D editor for
          that model. Users can adjust rooms, walls, doors, windows, objects and
          the roof, with full undo and redo. It is built on{" "}
          <a href="https://www.babylonjs.com/">Babylon.js</a>, and we designed
          its architecture.
        </p>
        <p>
          The hard part was making editing fast. We designed the heuristic
          algorithms and interaction model behind it, including{" "}
          <strong>bump-outs</strong>, <strong>wall merging</strong> and{" "}
          <strong>vertex merging</strong>. When someone moves a wall or a
          corner, the editor works out what they intend: it pushes part of a
          wall out into a bump-out, merges walls that line up into one, and
          joins corners that meet. The whole floor plan updates in a single
          move, where a generic vector editor would need many separate edits. As
          with all our client work, the editor and its algorithms belong to
          Yembo.
        </p>
        <figure class="diagram-figure">
          <FloorPlanDiagram />
          <figcaption>
            An illustration of the idea: drag one wall, and the rooms on both
            sides, the connected wall and the door update together.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <h3>Mobile apps, from React Native to native</h3>
        <p>
          We brought Yembo's web SaaS platform to phones as a React Native app,
          and we develop and support it alongside the web platform. Now, with
          the help of AI, we are rewriting it as native applications:{" "}
          <strong>iOS in Swift</strong> and <strong>Android in Kotlin</strong>.
        </p>

        <h2>Keeping a large codebase modern</h2>
        <p>
          A platform movers and insurers rely on has to keep moving without
          breaking. Staying on modern technology is part of our responsibility,
          not an occasional project:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>
              Migrated the large codebases we work on from JavaScript and Redux
              to TypeScript and TanStack Query
            </strong>{" "}
            — safer changes through static types, and simpler, more consistent
            data fetching and caching
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Continuous refactoring</strong> of the applications and
            modules we are responsible for, improving their architecture while
            features keep shipping
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Automated end-to-end tests with Playwright</strong>, so
            refactoring and new features don't break what already works
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <strong>It pays off in the era of AI-assisted development.</strong> We
          have always kept the code easy for people to work with: static types,
          consistent patterns, clear module boundaries and automated tests. It
          turns out the same qualities make it easy to develop with AI. Types
          and tests give AI coding tools the context to make the right change,
          and give our engineers a fast way to verify it.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>We set up the codebase for AI development.</strong> We add
          skills that teach AI coding tools how the codebase is organized, speed
          up the linters, and add command-line tools that let AI run checks and
          see the results for itself. With this feedback loop, AI can carry a
          feature through to completion, and our team develops faster.
        </p>

        <h2>What it shows</h2>
        <p>
          This is how we prefer to work with every client: as part of the team,
          owning the parts we're responsible for, rather than renting out
          developers. We bring full-stack engineering for SaaS platforms,
          complex features like live video and 3D, mobile apps, experience
          turning AI and prototypes into production features, and AI-assisted
          development on a codebase we keep modern for the long term.
        </p>

        <LeadBlock title="Looking for a long-term engineering partner?">
          We work as one accountable team alongside yours — product design,
          development, QA, and delivery — and stay as long as the product does.
          Tell us about your product and we will propose a team, a delivery plan
          and a first milestone.
        </LeadBlock>
      </div>
    </article>
    <ContactBanner />
  </div>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
